@meta
id: 12-03
title: Drill — search, then fix
chapter: 12
type: drill
skills: search-slash
par: 20
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: Ctrl+F, type, Enter, Escape, click, edit
open: http.config.ts

@brief
Eight times: the retry count near the bottom of the config should be 5,
not 2. Get there with a search, change the digit, save.

Never touch a motion key. The whole point is that the distance to the
line stops mattering.

@keys
| `/text` `Enter` | jump to the next match |
| `f` `x` | to the next `x` on this line |
| `r` | replace one character |

@hints
One search gets you onto the line. The digit is at the end of it.
--
`/retries` `Enter`, then `f2` to hop onto the digit, then `r5` to
overwrite it.

@solution
/retries<Enter>  $  r5  :wq<Enter>

Seventeen keystrokes, and it would be seventeen if the file were four
thousand lines long. That is the property you are drilling: search time
is independent of distance, so you stop thinking about where in the file
things are.

By rep eight you should be typing `/retries` without deciding to. The
rhythm is: name the thing, Enter, edit. Most edits in a real file start
that way.

@start http.config.ts
export const httpConfig = {
  baseUrl: 'https://api.example.com',
  userAgent: 'initech-order-service/2.4.1',
  keepAlive: true,
  maxSockets: 64,
  compression: 'gzip',
  proxy: undefined,
  headers: {
    accept: 'application/json',
    'content-type': 'application/json',
  },
  timeouts: {
    connectMs: 2000,
    requestMs: 8000,
    idleMs: 15000,
  },
  telemetry: {
    enabled: true,
    sampleRate: 0.25,
    endpoint: 'https://otel.example.com/v1/traces',
  },
  circuitBreaker: {
    failureThreshold: 5,
    resetMs: 30000,
  },
  retries: 2,
  retryDelayMs: 400,
};

@expected http.config.ts
